<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-barrier">
  <h3>Barrier</h3>
  <p>The skin’s protective lipid layer. When compromised, products absorb poorly and irritation rises — cream alone cannot fix a broken barrier.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-sebum">
  <h3>Sebum</h3>
  <p>The skin’s natural oil. Excess production can clog pores; the goal is balance, not stripping oil away entirely.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-pih">
  <h3>PIH</h3>
  <p>Post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation — dark marks left after acne inflammation. Needs melanin regulation and UV protection, not more harsh actives alone.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-melasma">
  <h3>Melasma</h3>
  <p>Hormonal and UV-driven pigmentation. Daily broad-spectrum protection matters as much as brightening actives.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-bha">
  <h3>BHA</h3>
  <p>Beta hydroxy acid (typically salicylic acid). Oil-soluble, so it can work inside the pore to clear congestion.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-aha">
  <h3>AHA</h3>
  <p>Alpha hydroxy acid (e.g. glycolic acid). Water-soluble surface exfoliation that supports smoother-looking texture.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-encapsulation">
  <h3>Encapsulation</h3>
  <p>A delivery approach that protects actives until application — improving stability and releasing fresher efficacy when you use the product.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-non-comedogenic">
  <h3>Non-comedogenic</h3>
  <p>Formulated to be less likely to clog pores — essential for acne-prone routines that still need moisture and SPF.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-pa">
  <h3>PA++++</h3>
  <p>A UVA protection rating used widely in Asia. More + signs indicate stronger UVA defence alongside SPF for UVB.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-acid-mantle">
  <h3>Acid mantle</h3>
  <p>The skin’s slightly acidic surface film that helps defend against microbes. High humidity and harsh cleansers can disrupt it.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-tewl">
  <h3>TEWL</h3>
  <p>Transepidermal water loss — moisture escaping through the skin. Spikes in dry winters when the barrier is under stress.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-humectant">
  <h3>Humectant</h3>
  <p>An ingredient that attracts and holds water in the skin (e.g. glycerin, saccharide isomerate).</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-emollient">
  <h3>Emollient</h3>
  <p>An ingredient that softens and smooths by filling gaps in the surface — cushion without necessarily feeling greasy.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-photostable">
  <h3>Photostable</h3>
  <p>A UV filter that holds up under sunlight instead of breaking down quickly — critical for real-world daytime wear.</p>
</article>
<article class="psr-glossary__term" id="term-efficacious">
  <h3>Efficacious concentration</h3>
  <p>A dose chosen because it can do the job — not a decorative sprinkle for the label.</p>
</article>
